# Holidays and observances, English.
#
# [time.holiday]: forms | rule | regions
#   rule:    fixed MM-DD                      the same date every year
#            nth N|last WEEKDAY MONTH [+-D]   the Nth (or last) weekday of a month, plus or minus days (mon..sun)
#            easter +-D                       days from Western Easter Sunday (Gregorian computus)
#            nearest WEEKDAY MM-DD            the weekday closest to a date
#   regions: us, gb or all (comma-separated). The recognizer's region selects the rows; all rows named all apply everywhere.
#
# Sources: United States federal holidays, 5 U.S.C. 6103; United Kingdom bank holidays, gov.uk/bank-holidays; the Western Christian calendar
# for the moveable feasts; the rest are the customary dates. Dates are the calendar day of the observance, not the day a weekend holiday is
# observed in lieu. Holidays that follow a lunar calendar (Eid, Diwali, Passover, Hanukkah, Ramadan, Lunar New Year) are not in this table.

[time.holiday]
New Year's Day, New Years Day | fixed 01-01 | all
New Year's Eve, New Years Eve | fixed 12-31 | all
Martin Luther King Jr. Day, Martin Luther King Jr Day, Martin Luther King Day, MLK Day | nth 3 mon 1 | us
Groundhog Day | fixed 02-02 | us
Valentine's Day, Valentines Day | fixed 02-14 | all
Presidents' Day, Presidents Day, President's Day, Washington's Birthday | nth 3 mon 2 | us
St. Patrick's Day, St Patrick's Day, Saint Patrick's Day | fixed 03-17 | all
